---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Anim from "../../components/Anim.astro";
import Code from "../../components/Code.astro";

const sample = `import { evalAllClusters, clustersOf, largestCluster } from "@open-rgs/pay-cluster";

const wins = evalAllClusters(grid, CLUSTER, { roles });

clustersOf(grid, "HIGH", roles);     // groups, for presentation
largestCluster(grid, "HIGH", roles); // biggest group size`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="@open-rgs/pay-cluster  - Connected groups"
  description="Pay-cluster: A wild belongs to every cluster it touches."
>
  <main>
    <p class="dim"><a href="/extension">&larr; extensions</a></p>
    <h1>@open-rgs/pay-cluster</h1>

    <p class="lede">A wild belongs to every cluster it touches.</p>

    <Anim kind="pay-cluster-wild" caption="The outlined wild is counted in the teal group and the amber one." />
    <Anim kind="pay-cluster-flood" caption="A flood fill from each real occurrence, spreading through neighbours." />
    <Anim kind="pay-cluster-diag" caption="Orthogonal only. Diagonals do not connect." />

    <h2 data-section="&sect; 1">Using it</h2>
    <Code code={sample} />

    <h2 data-section="&sect; 2">Why</h2>
    <p>Wilds are the whole difficulty. The fill runs per symbol and consumes only real matches - consume the wild for the first cluster and the second silently shrinks by one, with nothing on the board looking wrong. A cluster is never seeded from a wild, or a lone wild would invent wins.</p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
